# Rust
/target/
gametrimmer.db*

# Portable packaging output (scripts/package-portable.ps1)
/dist/

# Pre-release plans, audits, the project's own history and old git backups.
# Kept next to the code because that is where they are useful, but they are
# not part of the published project: they describe intentions rather than the
# shipped program, and a reader who found them here would reasonably take them
# for current guidance. Stored as a single compressed archive rather than
# loose files - see the extraction and warning notes inside it.
/docs/archive.7z
/docs/archive/

# The same reasoning for the loose ones: a dated audit or redesign plan is a
# snapshot of what was wrong on that day, and someone finding it in a release
# would read a fixed problem as a current one. They stay next to the code and
# out of the published tree.
/docs/codebase-audit-*.md
/docs/portability-audit.md
/docs/ui-redesign-plan-*.md

# Working notes about friction hit while building, not about the program.
/.papercuts.jsonl

